 =?UTF-8?q?measurement:=20reversal=20is=20not=20rewind,=20across=20five=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?carriers=20to=20the=20non-associative=20octonion=20loop?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measures, on srmech 0.9.0rc425 (registry 649, numpy absent, pure path), whether
reversing a relational path needs an INVERSION as well as an order-flip. Every
product / conjugate / modular step runs through a shipped op (cyclic_mod_add,
q8_mult, q8_conjugate, oct_mult, oct_conjugate, oct_torsor_act, oct_torsor_div,
cd_mult, cd_conjugate, associator, mod_mul, gcd); no abs() anywhere; exact
integers throughout.

Headlines:

* CHIRAL reversal is co-extensive with the FORWARD law on EVERY carrier — set
  equality, not merely equal counts — including the non-associative octonion
  unit loop. BARE reversal is not, except where the carrier is abelian.
* The FORWARD law is itself NOT total at 𝕆 (2752/4096), and the shortfall is
  exactly non-associativity: the law holds at a triple iff the associator of
  that triple vanishes, agreeing on 4096/4096. That reproduces the number the
  shipped associator docstring already documents (344/512 basis triples × 8
  sign combinations).
* SHIPPED-OP DEFECT: oct_torsor_act is an ANTI-action, not an action.
  (t<|g1)<|g2 == t<|(g2·g1) on 512/512, while the right-action law it
  documents holds on only 320/512 — exactly the commuting pairs of H. Its
  docstring calls T a "principal RIGHT torsor for H"; it is a torsor for H^op.
* The bare-reversal success RATE equals the group's commuting probability
  k(G)/|G|, so Gustafson's 5/8 theorem CAPS bare reversal at 5/8 for any
  non-abelian group. Q8 attains it exactly; T/I gives 3/8 (5184/13824).

